Non-standard linux and vim files that I use to make my life easier.

The root of this git repo is assumed to be your home directory.
In other words the "bin" directory is actually "~/bin"

Some of these are modifications from other authors so see each individual file for it's license.

== Git pre-commit hook ==

Repos under ~/repos with init.templateDir or symlinked hooks use
`.git-templates/hooks/pre-commit`. That hook reads ignore rules from:

* `<repo>/.git-hooks-ignorefile` (optional, usually not committed)
* `~/.git-hooks-ignorefile` (per developer; paths are relative to repo root)

Format: `path/relative/to/repo=Git::Hooks::IgnoreFile`

Use this for file types the hook does not classify (e.g. `conf/crontab.in`,
Helm `charts/*/templates/*.yaml`). Comment lines start with `#`.

